# M6.4 acceptance, run 2 of 3: restart with the chats of run 1, select and
# resume them, a chat with no session_id, a resume that fails and "Continue
# in new chat", and a sidecar crash in the middle of a reply. Run through
# tests/acceptance/m6.4.sh after run 1 (m6.4.steps), with the same HOME and
# fixture; this run opens /tmp/agentic-reader-m6.4/proj/paper.pdf again with
# a new fake sidecar log. Interface choices and the fake's replies are at the
# top of m6.4.steps.
#
# State after run 1, newest first:
#   BRAVO     "BRAVO one: summarize the paper in one line", 2 exchanges,
#             session sess-<id>
#   DOOMED    titled "Doomed renamed", 1 exchange, session
#             sess-doomed-<id>, which the fake cannot resume: the first prompt
#             after its resume fails with `error` process ("No conversation
#             found with session ID: sess-doomed-...") and closes the chat
#   FAILFIRST one user message, no reply, session_id null
#   ALPHA     2 exchanges, session sess-<id>
# Every selection below uses End, because each time the chat to open is the
# last entry.
#
# A message ending "#crash" makes the fake print "Working on it" and exit
# with status 3. SidecarClient restarts it about 1 s later and re-sends
# open_project; the selected chat must then be resumed (M5.1 carried note).
# m6.4-check.py run2 checks the order of new_chat/resume_chat/prompt in both
# sidecar processes, the transcripts and session ids.
wait 4

# At start the newest chat, BRAVO, is selected and resumed: the dropdown
# reads "BRAVO one: summarize the paper in one line", the view shows its
# transcript from disk: "BRAVO one: ...", "Answer 1 in this session. You
# said: BRAVO one: ...", "BRAVO two: back in this chat", "Answer 2 in this
# session. You said: BRAVO two: ...". No red notice.
shot restart-bravo

click 1040 90
wait 1

# The list survived the restart, newest first: "BRAVO one: ...",
# "Doomed renamed", "FAILFIRST one: this first reply fails #fail",
# "ALPHA one: what does the opening page of this paper say rega".
shot restart-list

key Escape
wait 1
key End
wait 2

# ALPHA selected: the dropdown reads "ALPHA one: what does the opening page
# of this paper say rega" (or as much as fits), the view shows its two
# exchanges ("ALPHA one: ...", "Answer 1 ...", "ALPHA two: and what is on
# page 2?", "Answer 2 ..."), nothing of BRAVO. No red notice.
shot alpha-resumed

click 1180 800
type ALPHA three: what did I ask first?
key Return
wait 3

# The follow-up goes to the resumed session: under the old exchanges,
# "ALPHA three: what did I ask first?" and "Answer 3 in this session. You
# said: ALPHA three: what did I ask first?. Earlier in this session you first
# asked: ALPHA one: what does the opening page of this paper say regarding
# our method?" with its cost line. "Answer 3" proves the same session.
shot alpha-follow-up

click 1040 90
wait 1
key Escape
wait 1
key End
wait 2

# FAILFIRST selected (it has no session_id): the dropdown reads "FAILFIRST
# one: this first reply fails #fail", the view shows that one user message
# and no reply. No red notice, no "cannot resume" mark, Send enabled.
shot failfirst-reopened

click 1180 800
type FAILFIRST two: try again
key Return
wait 3

# FAILFIRST works: "FAILFIRST two: try again" and "Answer 1 in this session.
# You said: FAILFIRST two: try again." under the first message. No red
# notice.
shot failfirst-recovered

click 1040 90
wait 1
key Escape
wait 1
key End
wait 2

# DOOMED selected: the dropdown reads "Doomed renamed", the view shows
# "DOOMED one: remember the word PLUM #doom" and "Answer 1 in this session.
# You said: DOOMED one: ...". No red notice yet (the resume is only known to
# have failed at the first prompt).
shot doomed-selected

click 1180 800
type DOOMED two: what word did I ask you to remember?
key Return
wait 3

# The resume failed. The transcript stays: "DOOMED one: ...", its answer,
# and "DOOMED two: what word did I ask you to remember?". The chat is marked
# "cannot resume" (in a notice in the view and/or the dropdown entry), and a
# "Continue in new chat" button shows in the chat pane. The view does not
# say "The chat was reopened" and no reply follows. The input is still at
# the bottom of the pane.
shot cannot-resume

key alt+c
wait 3
click 1180 800
type NEW one: continue where we left off
key Return
wait 3

# Continued in a new chat: the dropdown shows the new chat selected (not
# "Doomed renamed"). The view shows "NEW one: continue where we left off" and
# "Answer <n> in this session. You said: NEW one: continue where we left
# off." (n is 1, or 2 when the context prompt went out at once and its reply
# is shown above). The view does not show DOOMED's messages as this chat's
# own messages, except as part of a context prompt the app chose to show.
# No red notice.
shot continued

click 1040 90
wait 1

# The list, newest first: the new chat, "Doomed renamed" (possibly marked
# cannot resume), "FAILFIRST one: ...", "ALPHA one: ...", "BRAVO one: ...".
shot list-after-continue

key Escape
wait 1
key End
wait 2

# BRAVO selected again (it was resumed at start in this sidecar, so nothing
# is sent): its two exchanges show. No red notice.
shot bravo-before-crash

click 1180 800
type BRAVO three: this reply crashes the agent #crash
key Return
wait 6

# The sidecar crashed in the middle of the reply and was restarted: under
# "BRAVO three: this reply crashes the agent #crash", "Working on it" and the
# red "Agent stopped, restarting..." notice with "Send your message again."
# (the expected notice). The status bar's right field reads "Assistant
# ready" or a restart message, not "unavailable". BRAVO is still selected,
# its earlier exchanges still show.
shot after-crash

click 1180 800
type BRAVO four: are you still there?
key Return
wait 3

# BRAVO was resumed in the restarted sidecar: "BRAVO four: are you still
# there?" and "Answer 3 in this session. You said: BRAVO four: are you still
# there?. Earlier in this session you first asked: BRAVO one: summarize the
# paper in one line." No new red notice ("chat is not open" would be a
# failure).
shot bravo-after-restart

click 1040 90
wait 1
key Escape
wait 1
key End
wait 2
click 1180 800
type ALPHA four: after the restart
key Return
wait 3

# ALPHA, never opened in the restarted sidecar, was resumed when selected:
# the view shows its transcript ending with its three earlier exchanges (at
# least the newest, "ALPHA three: ..." and its answer, when scrolled to the
# bottom), then "ALPHA four: after the restart"
# and "Answer 4 in this session. You said: ALPHA four: after the restart.
# Earlier in this session you first asked: ALPHA one: ...". No red notice.
# tests/acceptance/m6.4.sh checks that this shot exists.
shot alpha-after-restart

key ctrl+q
wait 3
